<!-- The D. Ariz. complaint's Word styles and pleading paper: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in
     the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; LRCiv 7.1(b)(1) asks for a proportional face) at 13 pt
     (size 26 half points, LRCiv 7.1(b)(1)); Body Text and headings in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch: the
     numbered lines, LRCiv 7.1(b)(1) double spacing); single lines in 16 pt boxes (typst pitch-single). The page:
     letter, top margin 1 in, 27 numbered lines of 24 pt (LRCiv 7.1(b)(1): no more than 28), so the bottom margin is
     1 in too; left margin 1.5 in, right 1 in (LRCiv 7.1(b)(1): at least 1 1/2 and 1/2 inch). The line numbers 1 to 27
     are a text box in the header (rIdHdrLines), anchored to the page at the top margin, one exact 24 pt line each,
     ending 1.08 in from the page's left edge (typst number-column), so each sits on the baseline of its text line;
     the pleading rules are page borders (a double rule left of the text, a single rule right of it); the page number
     (rIdFtrAzd) is centered in a 16 pt line 8 pt below the text area, the line 48 pt above the page foot (960 twips:
     typst footer-descent 8 pt). docx/azd-complaint.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
